<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rustaq</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rustaq is a town in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a> on the inland side of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hajar-mountains">Hajar Mountains</a>, dominated by a large fort. In 1624 Ibadi scholars there elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nasir-ibn-murshid">Nasir ibn Murshid</a> as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imam</a>, founding the Ya'aruba dynasty, and the town served at several times as a seat of the imams and of the early Al Bu Said rulers. It is known for its hot springs and falaj irrigation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/rustaq.jpg" alt="Rustaq" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hans Birger Nilsen · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Al_Rustaq_Fort_(2)_(27255509348).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
